%I A399138 #15 Aug 23 2026 00:00:01
%S A399138 1,8,16,28,40,64
%N A399138 a(n) = maximum number of points in the n X n X n grid with no three of them collinear.
%C A399138 Collinear means collinear as points of R^3 (not modulo n); cf. A280537 for the "no four coplanar" analog.
%C A399138 Lower bounds for the next terms, with witness configurations in the attached file: a(7) >= 73, a(8) >= 93.
%C A399138 a(p) >= p^2 for every prime p, via the graph of an anisotropic binary quadratic form: {(x, y, Q(x,y) mod p) : 0 <= x,y < p} with Q = x^2 - d*y^2, d a quadratic non-residue, contains no three collinear points. For Q = x^2 + y^2 (which requires p == 3 (mod 4)) this is the construction of Por and Wood.
%C A399138 Every optimum found has the same layer profile along all three axes. For n = 2, 3, 4, 6 the two outer layers carry the planar maximum 2n and the inner ones 2n-2, giving a(n) = 2*n^2 - 2*n + 4; at n = 5 this profile is infeasible (two outer layers cannot both carry 2n points at any total) and a(5) = 40 has the uniform profile (8,8,8,8,8).
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019279">Certified exact values for the no-three-in-line problem in the three-dimensional grid</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="https://github.com/iwasborninbali/saturation">Programs, journals, witnesses and a verification protocol</a>, GitHub, 2026.
%H A399138 A. Por and D. R. Wood, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00453-006-0158-9">No-Three-in-Line-in-3D</a>, Algorithmica 47 (2007), 481-488.
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="/A399138/a399138.txt">Witness configurations for a(1)-a(6) and for the bounds a(7) >= 73, a(8) >= 93</a>
%F A399138 a(n) = Theta(n^2): the upper bound a(n) <= 2*n^2 is elementary (each of the n^2 axis-parallel lines carries at most two points; attained at n = 2), the lower bound Omega(n^2) is due to Por and Wood.
%e A399138 a(2) = 8: all eight points of the 2 X 2 X 2 cube may be taken, since no line contains three points of that grid.
%Y A399138 Cf. A000769 (the two-dimensional problem), A280537 (no four coplanar in the same grid), A157882.
%K A399138 nonn,more,hard,new
%O A399138 1,2
%A A399138 _Aleksei Kudriashov_, Aug 19 2026
